[I] Tools for network block devices

[T] nbd contains nbd-server and nbd-client for the Network Block Device
[T] protocol, which lets a computer access a remote storage device such as a
[T] disk or partition as if it were local, over TCP/IP. This allows e.g.
[T] remote booting, remote swap and network storage for diskless systems.

[U] https://nbd.sourceforge.io/

[A] Nbd Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

